# What does NOT get uploaded to Vercel.
#
# ⚠️ THE ENV LINES ARE LOAD-BEARING. Vercel falls back to .gitignore only while
# this file does not exist. The moment it does, every .gitignore rule stops
# applying — including the one keeping .env.local out — so the secrets would be
# uploaded into the deployment. Anything secret must be named here explicitly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.local.example

# Not imported by the app, and some of it is not ours to ship: the ProductOS
# material is licensed, the design export is a reference, and since worktrees
# started landing under .claude/ a deploy was carrying a second full checkout
# of the repo.
.claude/
productos/
saaf-ai/
docs/
scripts/
*.local.md

# The harvested candidate list is 4 MB+ and is read by nothing at runtime — only
# by scripts/qualify-boards.ts, which is excluded above. registry/boards.json is
# NOT excluded and must not be: ingest/run.ts reads it on every cron run.
registry/candidates.json

# ⚠️ THE BENCH CORPUS IS PERSONAL DATA AND MUST NEVER BE UPLOADED.
# bench/corpus/real/ holds nine of the founder's own résumés — full name, employer
# history, phone, email. They are gitignored, and the header above is exactly why
# that is not enough: this file existing means .gitignore no longer applies, so
# "it is gitignored" is the reasoning that ships them.
#
# Caught on 2026-09-14 while staging a deploy — the RUNBOOK's rsync had copied all
# nine into /tmp/saaf-deploy ready for upload. Nothing had leaked: the corpus
# arrived in 40cc807 on 2026-09-12 and the last deploy was 2026-09-09, so this was
# the first deploy that could have carried it.
#
# Read by nothing at runtime — only scripts/bench-*.ts, and scripts/ is already
# excluded above. The product's whole promise is that a résumé is parsed and
# dropped; shipping the founder's own into a public deployment would break it in
# the most literal way available.
bench/
